# Auto commit and push

After every modification to the project (code, assets, config, or content), always:

1. Stage the relevant changed files
2. Create a git commit with a concise message focused on the why
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch

Do this without waiting for the user to ask. Follow the existing git safety protocol (no force push to main/master, no config changes, no secrets, use HEREDOC for commit messages).
